Dynamic-array bounds checking
=============================

`new [n]int` yields a `&[]int` of length `n`. Out-of-bounds
indexing should be a runtime trap: the program halts via the
contract-check / panic path.

Today only the interpreter enforces bounds checks. Five
backends (llvm-host, svm-host, riscv64, riscv32, wasm32)
let OOB reads/writes silently succeed, reading garbage memory
or writing into adjacent allocations. TRISC is the closest
to correct — it traps some but not all of the cases (e.g.
the OOB-store case slips through). This is a real cross-
backend feature gap and one of the biggest remaining
soundness holes.

We pin the in-bounds happy-path here; the trapping cases
get a TODO until every backend traps uniformly. The expected
tests, once bounds checking is universal:

  - `a[len]` traps    — index equal to length
  - `a[100]` traps    — index past length
  - `a[-1]` traps     — negative index
  - `a[5] = 7` traps  — OOB store on a 3-element array

    module sysl.tests.lang_features

In-bounds reads return zero-init contents
-----------------------------------------

    #test
    test_in_bounds_read() -> unit
        val a: &[]int = new [5]int
        assert(a[0] == 0, s"a[0] should be 0, got ${a[0]}")
        assert(a[4] == 0, s"a[4] should be 0, got ${a[4]}")

In-bounds writes followed by reads
----------------------------------

    #test
    test_in_bounds_write_read() -> unit
        val a: &[]int = new [3]int
        a[0] = 1
        a[1] = 22
        a[2] = 333
        assert(a[0] == 1 && a[1] == 22 && a[2] == 333,
            s"a = [${a[0]},${a[1]},${a[2]}], expected [1,22,333]")

    // TODO: re-enable once uniform bounds-check trapping lands on every
    // backend (currently only the interpreter and TRISC partially honour
    // the OOB-traps contract):
    //
    //     #test(should_panic) test_index_equal_to_len()  -- a[3] on [3]int
    //     #test(should_panic) test_index_past_len()      -- a[100]
    //     #test(should_panic) test_negative_index()      -- a[-1]
    //     #test(should_panic) test_oob_store()           -- a[5] = 7
